#
# Name every pstop USB-NCM tether esp-pstop<N>, where N is the kernel's own
# usb<N> index (lowest free). Several units on one host therefore get distinct,
# predictable names -- esp-pstop0, esp-pstop1, ... -- with no per-unit
# registration, and the pstop-port profile (match esp-pstop*) picks each one up
# and puts it on the pstop-br bridge.
#
# Replaces the earlier 70-esp-pstop.link, which pinned a single fixed name
# (esp-pstop0) to the VID:PID: the second unit's rename hit EEXIST, stayed
# usb<N>, matched no profile and got no DHCP -- "only one USB Ethernet appears".
#
# Matches the app-mode device by VID:PID (303a:4001) on the USB parent, so it
# ignores download mode (303a:1001) and needs no ID_* imports. Sorted before
# 80-net-setup-link.rules, whose .link handling (including Ubuntu's
# 73-usb-net-by-mac.link -> enx<mac>) only applies while NAME is still empty.
# Install: sudo cp to /etc/udev/rules.d/ ; udevadm control --reload
SUBSYSTEM=="net", ACTION=="add", ATTRS{idVendor}=="303a", ATTRS{idProduct}=="4001", NAME="esp-pstop%n"
